subproblems.statement:
Let N, n ∈ ℕ and H = H^n = μHE[n] on ℝ^N = Euclidean N. Let μ be a measure on ℝ^N, M ⊆ ℝ^N and θ : ℝ^N → ℝ. Assume:
- M is H-null-measurable;
- θ(x) > 0 for every x ∈ M;
- θ is H-integrable on M ∩ K for every compact K ⊆ ℝ^N;
- μ(B) = ∫⁻_{M ∩ B} ofReal(θ) dH for every Borel B ⊆ ℝ^N;
- μ(s·A) = s^n μ(A) for every s > 0 and every set A ⊆ ℝ^N.
Then for every s > 0, H({w : w ∈ M, s·w ∉ M}) = 0 and H({w : s·w ∈ M, w ∉ M}) = 0.
